One-shot seed per open in BOTH dispatch modals, exactly as fix-round-3.md rules it. Added `const seededRef = React.useRef(false);` next to `analyzeSeq` in each modal and replaced each seed effect. routes/page.tsx (was deps `[open, routeSettings?.defaultStartTime, startTime]` with guard `!startTime`) is now:

  // Seed the default departure time once route settings arrive — one shot per
  // open, so an emptied field stays empty instead of snapping back to the
  // tenant default (see templates/[id]/page.tsx for the same shape).
  React.useEffect(() => {
    if (!open) {
      seededRef.current = false;
      return;
    }
    if (seededRef.current || !routeSettings?.defaultStartTime) return;
    seededRef.current = true;
    setStartTime(routeSettings.defaultStartTime);
  }, [open, routeSettings?.defaultStartTime]);

templates/[id]/page.tsx (was `React.useEffect(() => { if (routeSettings?.defaultStartTime && !startTime) { setStartTime(routeSettings.defaultStartTime); } }, [routeSettings?.defaultStartTime]);` — no `open` guard, `startTime` read but not a dep) is now byte-identical apart from the cross-reference comment naming routes/page.tsx:

  React.useEffect(() => {
    if (!open) {
      seededRef.current = false;
      return;
    }
    if (seededRef.current || !routeSettings?.defaultStartTime) return;
    seededRef.current = true;
    setStartTime(routeSettings.defaultStartTime);
  }, [open, routeSettings?.defaultStartTime]);

Trace on the clear path: operator empties the <input type="time"> → setStartTime("") → the seed effect's deps ([open, defaultStartTime]) are unchanged, so it does not re-run → the field stays empty and handleDispatch sends `startTime: startTime || undefined`. The debounced analyze effect (deps [open, routeId, startTime]) fires exactly once for the cleared value instead of twice, and `acknowledged` is reset once, not twice. On close the ref clears, so the next open re-seeds. Only the two briefed files were touched; no other hunk in either file was modified. Re the brief's "remove the eslint-disable there": the templates seed effect carried NO `// eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` in this tree (the only disable in that file is at the analyze effect, now line 375, and is untouched) — the new deps are exhaustive, so none was needed or added.
